  "evidence_summary": "CG actual mesh buffer fields: six complete ordinary bodies525bytes and two EH supports18bytes;205 executable owners,16 direct and15 indirect transfers, saved/disk byte equality. Index reader maps then multiplies, raw reads, current unmap/post-upload, mesh retained replacement, creator release. Vertex reader ignores BEA010 returned header, captures current declaration/factory slots separately, releases declaration temporary before stride read/map, uses rope.mvfm trailing skip, current mesh count at publication, creator release and completed-local-name-only EH. Raw BF02F0 passes its requested-count slot as actual-count output and debits current budget after return; no status checks or rollback. Existing actual D3D9 factories/cache/mesh/pools/companions reused. Strict worktree-only CC/CE/CF/CG CMake build passed both CTests. One actual RTX5090 HAL source fixture passed both index widths, two vertex names/GPU readbacks, retained map/creator on read failure and all eight canonical retirements. Source-parent fixture, no copied-original parent oracle, cold decode, device-loss, native ABI/FH3/SEH, tracked registration, main integration or gameplay claim. Old comments and correct compiler names preserved; descriptive names hypotheses. docs/NATIVE_MESH_BUFFER_FIELDS_CG.md; reports/native_mesh_buffer_fields_cg.json.",
